lahoma State University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2011-05-04","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View from public campus walkways; protect the planted topiary by staying outside landscaped beds.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"proud-and-immortal","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Proud and Immortal","title":"Meet the horse sculptures","subtitle":"Saturday midday · east side of the Student Union","notes":"Circle back to the Union’s east side and take time to look closely at Marrita Black’s mare-and-colt sculpture from the plaza.","short_summary":"A named public-art stop outside the Union.","evidence_claim":"OSU’s public-art map places Marrita Black’s Proud and Immortal on the east side of the Student Union at 110 S. Hester Street.","source_url":"https://museum.okstate.edu/site-files/documents/public-art-map-sculpture-walk-2022.pdf","source_title":"Public Art Map: Sculpture Walk | OSU Museum of Art","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor artwork on the Student Union grounds; observe from public paths and do not climb on the sculpture.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"dna-iv","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"DNA IV","title":"See DNA IV at McKnight","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · McKnight Center plaza","notes":"Walk to the north side of the McKnight Center and view Bill Barrett’s bronze sculpture before checking the venue’s current calendar.","short_summary":"A permanent bronze work in OSU’s public-art collection.","evidence_claim":"OSU identifies DNA IV as a permanent Bill Barrett sculpture at the McKnight Center and part of the OSU Museum of Art collection.","source_url":"https://news.okstate.edu/magazines/state-magazine/articles/2019/winter/amplifying_art.html","source_title":"Amplifying Art | Oklahoma State University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2019-12-02","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The sculpture is outdoors; performance access and ticketing are separate, so check the McKnight Center calendar for any event plans.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"osu-museum-of-art","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"OSU Museum of Art","title":"Make an art-museum stop downtown","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · 720 S. Husband Street","notes":"Choose a current exhibition, give yourself time to look closely, and use the museum’s photography guidance before taking pictures.","short_summary":"A free downtown OSU museum visit.","evidence_claim":"The OSU Museum of Art lists free admission, Tuesday–Saturday gallery hours of 11 a.m.–4 p.m, and its address at 720 S. Husband Street.","source_url":"https://museum.okstate.edu/visit","source_title":"Visit | OSU Museum of Art","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Admission is always free. Gallery hours are Tuesday–Saturday, 11 a.m.–4 p.m.; closed Sunday and Monday.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"botanic-garden-at-osu","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"The Botanic Garden at Oklahoma State University","title":"Finish on the garden trails","subtitle":"Sunday morning · 3300 W. 6th Street","notes":"Take the walking trails and display gardens at an unhurried pace; pick up the visitor guide if you want named garden features.","short_summary":"A 100-acre OSU garden with trails and displays.","evidence_claim":"OSU describes The Botanic Garden as a 100-acre site with walking trails and display gardens, open 6 a.m.–8 p.m. March through October.","source_url":"https://extension.okstate.edu/programs/botanic-garden",